// The type checks: idc.py's assertions from gen_stmt/gen_expr/gen_binop,
// moved into the language. They are assertions on results ../../type_of/ already
// computes for codegen, and they get their type facts from ../../registry/ rather
// than from a new if-chain.
//
// The walk is over the whole node store, not over the function tree. That is
// sound here and nowhere else: id's rule that a name has one type
// program-wide means type_of(e) needs no scope, so a node can be judged
// wherever it sits. It also means each node is judged exactly once, including
// the ones inside `else if` chains, which a tree walk has to be careful about.
//
// Two things are NOT judged, deliberately:
//   * a type the compiler could not work out (ty_known == 0). An asm
//     function's return type is one, because the driver registers asm symbols
//     after check_program() runs. Reporting on an unknown type is how a check
//     invents diagnostics; staying quiet is how it stays trustworthy.
//   * an empty list literal as a value, which has no type of its own -- it
//     takes the one the context wants. chk_arr judges the context instead.

// The entry point. check_program()'s own block is full -- the chkfail export
// plus two calls -- so the check families chain instead of each taking a slot
// there; names/'s check_scopes() calls this one. It carries names/'s per-file
// rule along with it for the same reason.
check_rest() {
  check_files();
  check_shape();
  tc_all();
} return void;

tc_all() {
  init_tyreg();
  tc_nodes();
} return void;

tc_nodes() {
  int i = 0;
  while(i < len((import nkind))) {
    tc_node(i);
    i = i + 1;
  }
} return void;
